Food Safety Inspection | Palle Vindhu, Hitech City 
 CMC Food Safety Officers conducted an inspection at Palle Vindhu, Hitech City, to review food safety and hygiene practices. 
 Good practices observed: 
 • Hairnets and aprons used by food handlers 
 • Water testing and medical fitness certificates maintained 
 • No synthetic colours or Ajinomoto used 
 • FOSTAC supervisors deployed 
 • No stored/stale or expired food observed 
 • Proper pest control practices and records maintained 
 • Regular cleaning schedules followed 
 • Raw materials properly labelled 
 Areas requiring improvement: 
 • Uneven wash-area surface causing water accumulation at some points 
 • Drain mesh to be installed 
 FoSCoS Score: 102/110 (93%) 
 The establishment was advised to address the observed deficiencies and continue maintaining good food safety and hygiene standards. 
 #TeamCMC #FoodSafety #SafeFood #Cyberabad 
