Food Safety Inspection | Ideal Kitchen, Beeramguda 
 CMC Food Safety Officers conducted an inspection at Ideal Kitchen, Beeramguda, Ameenpur, to review food safety and hygiene practices. 
 Non-compliances observed: 
 • Kitchen found small, congested and not properly cleaned 
 • Semi-prepared batters and chutneys stored close to a brooming stick 
 • Medical, pest control, water testing, food testing and packaging records were not available 
 • Artificial food colours were in use and discarded on the spot 
 • Prepared rice items including sambar rice, lemon rice, pulihora and mudda pappu-avakaya were kept open 
 • Batters were not properly labelled 
 • Open drain and broken flooring in the grinding area causing water stagnation and odour 
 • Exhausts were not cleaned properly 
 FoSCoS Score: 58/92 (63%) 
 A notice was issued for the observed violations, with directions to rectify the deficiencies and improve food safety and hygiene standards. 
 #TeamCMC #FoodSafety #SafeFood #Cyberabad 
