Food Safety Inspection | Babai Hotel, Madinaguda 
 CMC Food Safety Officers conducted an inspection at Babai Hotel, Madinaguda, to review food safety and hygiene practices. 
 Good practices observed: 
 • Pest control, packaging and water testing records were available. 
 Non-compliances observed: 
 • Medical records of food handlers and food testing records were not available 
 • Uneven flooring causing water stagnation and odour in the dishwashing area 
 • Semi-prepared foods such as poori and poornam were not labelled 
 • Food waste was not cleared from drains 
 • Exhaust was greasy and required cleaning 
 • Broken flooring observed at some places in the kitchen 
 FoSCoS Score: 69/98 (71%) 
 A notice was issued for the observed violations, with directions to rectify the deficiencies and maintain required food safety and hygiene standards. 
