Food Safety Check | Jaaju Kitchen & Bar 
 CMC Food Safety Officers conducted an inspection at Jaaju Kitchen & Bar, Madinaguda, to check food safety, hygiene and compliance standards. 
 Good practices observed: 
 • Good personal hygiene maintained by food handlers 
 • Pest control, annual medical and water testing records available 
 • Semi-prepared food items properly labelled 
 Areas requiring improvement: 
 • Food testing and packaging records not available 
 • Food waste observed in drains and an open drain near the dishwashing area 
 • Damaged gasket in the non-veg chiller requiring replacement 
 • Water clogging in the dishwashing sink 
 • Exhausts near stoves and freezer require proper cleaning 
 FoSCoS Score: 82/102 (80%) 
 The management was instructed to rectify the observed deficiencies and maintain required food safety and hygiene standards. 
