Food Safety Inspection | Antera Kitchen & Bar 
 Food Safety Officers of CMC conducted an inspection at Antera Kitchen & Bar, Madinaguda, to assess compliance with food safety and hygiene standards. 
 Good practices observed: 
 • TPC meter available for monitoring cooking oil quality. 
 • Probe thermometer in use. 
 • Records of medical fitness, food & water testing, packaging, pest control, calibration and RUCO maintained. 
 • Food handlers trained under FoSTaC. 
 • Pallets used for proper storage. 
 • Meshes fitted to kitchen doors and the non-vegetarian cutting area. 
 • Food items properly labelled. 
 Areas requiring improvement: 
 • Kitchen and store room doors should be fitted with a proper self-closing mechanism. 
 • Cleaning frequency behind cooking stoves needs to be increased. 
 FoSCoS Score: 100/106 (94%) 
 An Improvement Notice has been issued to address the identified observations and ensure continued compliance with food safety standards. 
 #TeamCMC #FoodSafety #SafeFood #Cyberabad 
