Food Safety Inspection | Pista House 
 Food Safety Officers of CMC conducted an inspection at Nestham Enterprises (Pista House), RC Puram, to assess compliance with food safety and hygiene standards. 
 Good practices observed: 
 • Personal hygiene maintained by food handlers. 
 • FSSAI license displayed prominently at the premises. 
 Major observations: 
 • Houseflies in the bakery section and fruit flies on stored carrots. 
 • No hot water provision in one of the dishwashing areas. 
 • Kitchen windows kept open. 
 • Food items not labelled with commodity names. 
 • Marinated biryani mix assigned a three-day shelf life without supporting technical evidence. 
 • Drains were not adequately cleaned, with food waste observed. 
 • Medical fitness, pest control, water testing, food testing and packaging records were not available. 
 • Water leakage observed inside the walk-in chiller. 
 • Rusting observed in a refrigerator. 
 FoSCoS Score: 72/104 (70%) 
 An Improvement Notice has been issued directing the Food Business Operator to rectify the identified deficiencies and ensure compliance with food safety standards. 
 #TeamCMC #FoodSafety #SafeFood #Cyberabad 
