Food Safety Inspection | Coal Spark 
 Food Safety Officers of CMC conducted an inspection at Coal Spark, Madhapur, to assess compliance with food safety and hygiene standards. 
 Good practices observed: 
 • Food handlers using hairnets and gloves. 
 • Water quality testing carried out. 
 • Natural colour extracts used in food preparation. 
 • FoSTaC-certified supervisors available at the premises. 
 • No expired food items or pest activity observed in the kitchen. 
 • Regular cleaning schedule maintained. 
 • FIFO and FEFO practices followed for food storage. 
 Areas requiring improvement: 
 • Water seepage and flaking observed on the store room walls. 
 • Pest activity noticed in a steamer kept under maintenance. 
 • Hot water sterilisation of utensils was not being followed. 
 • Rust observed on freezer racks, requiring corrective action to prevent contamination. 
 FoSCoS Score: 89/106 (84%) 
 An Improvement Notice has been issued directing the Food Business Operator to address the identified observations and ensure compliance with food safety standards. 
 #TeamCMC #FoodSafety #SafeFood #Cyberabad 
