Food Safety Inspection Drive 
 Establishment: Alsaba Restaurant 
 Gachibowli 
 09.07.2026 
 As part of routine food safety inspections across Cyberabad, CMC Food Safety teams inspected Alsaba Restaurant. 
 Good Practices 
 • No synthetic food colours found in use 
 • Food handlers were using hairnets 
 Key Observations 
 • Meat not stored under proper conditions in the freezer 
 • Improper wash area with water stagnation; unhygienic worker washrooms and fly movement observed 
 • No hot water sanitisation of utensils 
 • Rumali roti prepared adjacent to unclean washrooms with fly infestation 
 • Slaughtering area found unhygienic, with no separate containers for leftover chicken 
 • Water testing reports and medical fitness certificates of food handlers were not available 
 Action Initiated 
 • Action has been initiated to suspend the FSSAI licence. 
 • The restaurant has been directed to remain closed until all identified violations are rectified and compliance with food safety standards is verified. 
 Hygiene Assessment 
 69/150 Marks (46%) 
