Food Safety Inspection Drive | Moosapet 
 Location: Udupi Upahar, Moosapet 
 Date: 26.05.2026 
 As part of continuous food safety monitoring across Cyberabad, CMC Food Safety teams conducted an inspection at the above establishment. 
 Violations Identified: 
 • Slippery kitchen flooring observed 
 • Kitchen drain found clogged with food waste 
 • Cooked veg biryani, cooked rice, batters, paneer, manchurian, and dough improperly stored in freezer 
 • Storage containers found untidy 
 • Wash area maintained in unhygienic condition 
 • Frozen food not thawed hygienically 
 • Cockroach infestation and flies observed in kitchen area 
 • Food handlers found without hairnets and masks 
 • Medical records and water analysis reports not produced during inspection 
 • Establishment found operating with expired food license 
 Action Taken: 
 • Premises closed due to operation with expired license 
 • Stale veg biryani and manchurian discarded immediately 
 • Hygiene Score: 40 / 116 
 Hygiene Score Criteria: 
 Above 90% – Good 
 50% to 90% – Improvement Notice 
 Below 50% – Show Cause Notice 
 CMC will continue regular food safety inspections across restaurants, kitchens, eateries, and food establishments to strengthen hygiene standards and public health safety across Cyberabad. 
 Citizens can report food safety concerns through the MyCURE App or by tagging 
 @CMC_Offcl 
 on X/Twitter for prompt field inspection and necessary action. 
 Safe Food. Clean Kitchens. Healthier Cyberabad. 
